Mounting S3 Bucket on to VM
==============================
=> Create an S3 Bucket with Versioning Enabled
mount-s3 flipkart-ml-training-kastro

=> Upload 2-3 files into the bucket

=> Create an S3 File System
Open "flipkart-ml-training-kastro" bucket
Go to File systems - new tab (or Access Points → File systems)
Click Create file system ----> File system name: flipkart-ml-filesystem ----> Create

Note the file system ID

=> Launch an EC2 Instance - Amazon Linux 2023, Attach IAM Role with S3 Full Access Policy

=> Mount the S3 File System on EC2
Install Mountpoint for Amazon S3:
sudo dnf install -y mount-s3

Create a mount directory:
mkdir ~/s3-mount

Mount the bucket:
mount-s3 flipkart-ml-training-kastro ~/s3-mount

Verify:
df -h

ls ~/s3-mount
You will see the files in bucket

Create a test file:
echo "Hello S3" > ~/s3-mount/test.txt
Go to bucket and refresh, you will see "test.txt" file

Also, upload an object in S3 bucket ----> Goto VM and verify using "ls" command

=> Unmount on the EC2 instance:
umount ~/s3-mount

S3 → flipkart-ml-training-kastro → File systems tab → Select flipkart-ml-filesystem → Delete
EC2 → Terminate flipkart-ml-worker
S3 → Empty and delete flipkart-ml-training-kas
